Helion UI is an independent experimental implementation. It is not affiliated
with Microsoft, Avalonia, the Vello project, or Linebender. No Vello binary or
source implementation is embedded or linked. Sparse-strip design ideas and
primary references are acknowledged in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. The original
vector alphabet is authored as JavaScript geometry; no external font files,
brand logos, images, dependencies or hosted services are included.


Typography release 0.3.0
------------------------
The source distribution does not include font binaries, downloaded/system fonts,
font data URLs, or repackaged third-party font outlines. The normal showcase
requests Noto Sans Regular, SemiBold and Italic from public URLs pinned to the
notofonts/noto-fonts v20201206-phase3 tag. Font rights/notices are supplied by that
upstream distribution: https://github.com/notofonts/noto-fonts/tree/v20201206-phase3 .
Applications can instead load fonts they supply themselves through local File
objects or configured same-origin URLs. Respect each font's own terms.

The OpenType parser, retained text plan packer, GPU text/cache implementation and
the small synthetic font fixture builder are authored for this experiment. The
fixture builder uses simple original test geometry; it is not a bundled UI font.
OpenType specifications and HarfBuzz conceptual documentation were consulted; no
HarfBuzz or third-party font rasterizer implementation is linked.

Workbench release 0.9.0
-----------------------
The editor, docking, and numeric model code is independently authored for Helion.
No Monaco, CodeMirror, LSP server, third-party editor, or docking runtime is embedded.
The workbench requests Noto Sans Mono Regular from the same pinned runtime source
release, or uses a local font selected by the user. No font binary is distributed.

Dynamic workspace release 0.10.0
--------------------------------
The data-source, virtualized list/tree, action bridge, and embedded-presenter code
are independently authored for Helion. No additional font files or upstream UI
framework runtime is redistributed. The visible playground is retained Helion UI;
JavaScript execution and OS/browser service bridges remain host facilities.

Template/theme additions are independently authored. Fluent, WinUI, WPF and macOS
references identify inspiration and interoperability concepts, not affiliation or
certification. No native OS theme assets or font binaries are redistributed.

Typography 0.15
----------------
Generated Unicode 16.0 property data is covered by the accompanying
src/typography/UNICODE-LICENSE.txt. HarfBuzz 10.2.0 and ICU 76 are comparison
oracles in development tools only; no HarfBuzz/ICU binary or font is linked into
runtime applications. Script-specific mark ordering and shaping behavior were
informed by the HarfBuzz sources and Unicode/OpenType specifications. Reference
material and associated notice are in docs/HARFBUZZ-REFERENCE-NOTICE.txt.
